{"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Customizing Your C Code for Swift","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because structures in C can’t have methods, property accessors, or custom initializers,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you often need to write such functionality using global functions. Structures in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Swift can declare methods, property accessors, and initializers. You use the "},{"code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"macro to group together related global functions into a single structure type that’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"imported into Swift.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Apply CF_SWIFT_NAME to Related Functions","anchor":"Apply-CFSWIFTNAME-to-Related-Functions","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The example below shows several functions that are all related to a "},{"code":"Color","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro is applied to each function, giving each one a new name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"for Swift that’s nested together under the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Color","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type:"}]},{"syntax":"occ","code":["Color ColorCreateWithCMYK(float c, float m, float y, float k) CF_SWIFT_NAME(Color.init(c:m:y:k:));","","float ColorGetHue(Color color) CF_SWIFT_NAME(getter:Color.hue(self:));","void ColorSetHue(Color color, float hue) CF_SWIFT_NAME(setter:Color.hue(self:newValue:));","","Color ColorDarkenColor(Color color, float amount) CF_SWIFT_NAME(Color.darken(self:amount:));","","extern const Color ColorBondiBlue CF_SWIFT_NAME(Color.bondiBlue);","","Color ColorGetCalibrationColor(void) CF_SWIFT_NAME(getter:Color.calibration());","Color ColorSetCalibrationColor(Color color) CF_SWIFT_NAME(setter:Color.calibration(newValue:));"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The argument you pass to the "},{"code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro uses the same syntax as the "},{"code":"#selector","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expression. You use ","type":"text"},{"code":"self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" argument to refer to the instance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that the method belongs to."}]},{"anchor":"Import-Related-Functions-into-Swift","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Import Related Functions into Swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Here’s how Swift imports the related functions above into a single type:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["extension Color {","    init(c: Float, m: Float, y: Float, k: Float)","","    var hue: Float { get set }","","    func darken(amount: Float) -> Color","","    static var bondiBlue: Color","","    static var calibration: Color","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can’t reorder or change the number of arguments for type members imported","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"using the ","type":"text"},{"code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift"],"title":"Language Interoperability with C and C++","generated":true,"anchor":"Language-Interoperability-with-C-and-C++"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro to group functions that have related behavior.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"kind":"article","references":{"Swift-PageImage-card.png":{"type":"image","alt":"An orange Swift logo on a gradient background.","identifier":"Swift-PageImage-card.png","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/com.apple.Swift\/Swift-PageImage-card@2x.png","traits":["2x","light"]},{"url":"\/images\/com.apple.Swift\/Swift-PageImage-card~dark@2x.png","traits":["2x","dark"]}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift":{"title":"Using Imported C Structs and Unions in Swift","abstract":[{"text":"Learn how Swift represents imported C structures and unions, including types with","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bitfields and unnamed fields."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","kind":"article"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","kind":"article","title":"Using Imported C Functions in Swift","role":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to call imported functions that are declared in a C header."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Build apps using a powerful open language.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift","title":"Swift","kind":"symbol","images":[{"identifier":"Swift-PageImage-card.png","type":"card"}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift","role":"article","title":"Using Imported C Macros in Swift","abstract":[{"text":"Use imported C-defined macros as constants.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift","type":"topic","kind":"article"}}}